{"name":"Pappardelle Noodle","hex":"#f9ebcc","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"pappardelle","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A broad form of fettuccine, or a narrow form of lasagne, traditionally eaten with a meat sauce (especially one made with hare)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pappardelle"},{"term":"noodle","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A string or flat strip of pasta or other dough, usually cooked (at least initially) by boiling, and served in soup or in a dry form mixed with a sauce and other ingredients.","An object which is long and thin like a noodle (sense 1).\n  Ellipsis of pool noodle (“a long, slender tube or rod, extruded from buoyant foam and usually brightly coloured, used as an exercise tool or toy in swimming pools”)."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A person with poor judgment; a fool.","The brain; the head."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/noodle"}],"entries":[{"title":"Pappardelle","blocks":[{"text":"Pappardelle are large, very broad, flat pasta, similar to wide fettuccine, originating from the Tuscany region of Italy. The fresh types are two to three centimetres wide and may have fluted edges, while dried egg pappardelle have straight sides."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/Pappardelle.jpg/330px-Pappardelle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pappardelle","wikidata":"Q20041"},{"title":"Noodles","blocks":[{"text":"Noodles are a type of food typically made from unleavened dough which is rolled flat and cut, stretched, or extruded into long strips or strings. Noodles are a staple food in many cultures and made into a variety of shapes. The most common noodles are those derived from Chinese cuisine or Italian cuisine. Italian noodles are generally referred to as pasta. In Chinese cuisine, the overarching term for noodles is 麵, which refers specifically to dough-based noodles made from wheat or other grain-based dough. Chinese noodles also include another category, called 粉 (fěn), which are not made by kneading dough but from a starch slurry, such as rice noodles, and cellophane noodles. These are not made from wheat dough, but are still regarded as noodles in English due to their physical form and culinary role."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Dalian_Liaoning_China_Noodlemaker-01.jpg/330px-Dalian_Liaoning_China_Noodlemaker-01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Noodles","wikidata":"Q192874"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/Pappardelle_pomodoro_e_basilico.jpg/120px-Pappardelle_pomodoro_e_basilico.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/Pappardelle_pomodoro_e_basilico.jpg/250px-Pappardelle_pomodoro_e_basilico.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/Pappardelle_pomodoro_e_basilico.jpg/120px-Pappardelle_pomodoro_e_basilico.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APappardelle_pomodoro_e_basilico.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Lamb_Pappardelle.jpg/120px-Lamb_Pappardelle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Lamb_Pappardelle.jpg/250px-Lamb_Pappardelle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Lamb_Pappardelle.jpg/120px-Lamb_Pappardelle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.